It’s powerful to hear how widespread and impactful adolescent depression can be. What I’m noticing here is that while there’s a lot of awareness now around youth mental health, stigma still lingers—especially among teens who might feel they’re “not supposed” to struggle or that asking for help makes them weak.  

That brings me to an important point: **seeking support isn’t weakness—it’s courage**. When a teenager says, "I don't feel like myself anymore," or "I’ve stopped enjoying things I used to love"—that’s not a sign of failure;
